  "prompt": "What is the VAT rate on importation of goods used to manufacture export products?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe VAT rate on the importation of goods used to manufacture export products is 12%.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is established under Section 107 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that a value-added tax equivalent to twelve percent (12%) shall be levied on every importation of goods.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor businesses importing goods to be used in the manufacture of export products, they will incur a VAT of 12% at the time of importation. This VAT can potentially be recovered through input tax credits if the business is VAT-registered and the goods are used in taxable activities, including export sales, which may be zero-rated under certain conditions.",
